  "body": "Found in the review read of PR #3604 (Refs #3589).\n\n**Now:** `crates/ui/tests/trace_composite.rs` and `crates/ui/tests/trace_parity.rs` call `device_for_test` in each test. The tests run in parallel test threads. Two or more wgpu devices can be alive at the same time in one process. This is the same hazard that #3589 suspects for the lib tests.\n\n**Pattern to copy:** `crates/ui/tests/gpu_render.rs` has `GPU_TEST_LOCK` and one shared device in a `OnceLock`.\n\n**Also:** three `#[ignore]`d lib tests reach the GPU with no guard (`tests/guide_images.rs`, `tests/review_1710_evidence.rs`, `viewport_bar_tooltip_tests.rs`). They run together only with `--ignored`. Give them the guard of #3604.\n\n**Done when:** each test of the two integration binaries takes one lock or uses one shared device, and the three ignored lib tests take `gpu_guard()`.\n",
